      "direct_effect": 0,
      "id": "ET02",
      "note": "order_month's WH1 boost is a genuine summer (Jun-Aug) effect, deliberately disjoint from pattern E04's winter [12,1,2] window."
    },
    {
      "apparent_feature": "acquisition_channel=paid_search",
      "confounded_by": [
        "discount_pct"
      ],
      "direct_effect": 0,
      "id": "ET03",
      "note": "A proxy/mediator trap, not a pure non-causal assignment artifact like ET01/ET02/ET04: acquisition_channel has zero direct effect of its own, but it does causally shift discount_pct (a real, independently-discoverable DECISION_TIME feature), which then genuinely reduces margin. Tests whether a candidate condition correctly attributes the effect to discount_pct rather than to the correlated channel proxy."
    },
    {
      "apparent_feature": "payment_method=gift_card",
      "confounded_by": [
        "product_tier"
      ],
      "direct_effect": 0,
      "id": "ET04",
      "note": "Gift-card usage skews toward premium/luxury tier (upsell/gifting behavior). Deliberately independent of pattern E06's device_type=mobile trigger \u2014 the earlier device-linked wiring this trap was audited against created partial overlap with E06's real effect; product_tier does not appear in any pattern's condition."
    },
    {
      "apparent_feature": "coupon_used=true",
      "confounded_by": [
        "quantity"
      ],
      "direct_effect": 0,
      "id": "ET05",
      "note": "E05 is a genuine interaction; the main effect is a trap. The live mechanism is quantity<=1, chosen because it affects gross_revenue/base_cost/payment_fee directly rather than through the same weak, multi-step complexity->Bernoulli path ET01 relies on \u2014 an earlier version tried a customer_segment/items_in_cart pathway here and it was real but too faint to detect reliably. Independent of ET03's discount_pct pathway \u2014 the two traps are independently toggleable, not two labels on one shared code path \u2014 and disjoint from pattern E02's quantity>=5 trigger."
    }
  ],
